@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage with browser-local digital signing for sample coffee receipts and gift vouchers. No server or build is required to compile the page; serve the files over HTTPS (or localhost) for Web Crypto access.
+
+The page prefers ML-DSA-65 when the browser advertises support, then falls back to Ed25519 and ECDSA P-256/SHA-256. It stores a non-exportable private CryptoKey and its public verification key in IndexedDB. If persistent key storage fails, signing stays disabled. Clearing site data removes the signing identity.
+
+Signed JSON includes a version, algorithm, public-key fingerprint, exact payload string, and base64 signature. The signature binds those fields and a document-specific domain. Verification checks the signature against the saved public key, rejects foreign keys, and never accepts a public key supplied by an uploaded document. Editing JSON clears the displayed verification result. Download always saves the last generated document.
+
+These are local samples, not merchant-issued receipts or redeemable vouchers. Browser-controlled signing cannot establish that Daily Grind authorized a purchase or gift balance. Production issuance must use a merchant-controlled signer (without shipping merchant private keys to customers) and distribute independently authenticated merchant public keys to verifiers. Redemption and replay prevention require authoritative order/voucher state.
+
+Run automated cryptographic checks with:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/receipt-crypto.test.mjs
+```
+
+No dependencies are required. Tests cover receipt/voucher round trips, private-key export rejection, content/signature/metadata tampering, unknown keys, and invalid inputs. UI behavior and IndexedDB persistence were not manually tested in a browser.
